{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03OF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0012": "$$\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{k \\in K} \\mathcal{O}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{l \\in L} \\mathcal{O}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i}.\n$$", "MATH_0013": "$K$", "MATH_0014": "$V \\mapsto \\bigoplus_{k \\in K} \\mathcal{O}(V)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-ringed-site}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c1bcbebe4a89901374991164ba89df6b7becfcc7a7be935254a96a01735a3e43", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4657c57989456bae66b6c56802567c5cf204a5e4b3a40a7929547f6940bd9ec1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>ringed site<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, i.e., a site endowed with a\nsheaf of rings <MATH_0002>. A sheaf of <MATH_0003>-modules <MATH_0004> on\n<MATH_0005> is called <TEXTITOPEN_0002>quasi-coherent<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if for all\n<MATH_0006> there exists a covering\n<MATH_0007> of <MATH_0008> such that the restriction\n<MATH_0009> is isomorphic to the cokernel of\nan <MATH_0010>-linear map of free <MATH_0011>-modules\n<MATH_0012>\nThe direct sum over <MATH_0013> is the sheaf associated to the presheaf\n<MATH_0014> and similarly for the other.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3be0ae5f8bffccd21f63008e20f713ded458ddcb3095ee03afaacbfbd1011c34", "unit_id": "tag:03OH:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03OF", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:66a42082049353d0c1a524cf7955419332f9ebe03777a9f2cf21b1c64e5bbf88", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAlthough it is useful to be able to give a general definition as above\nthis notion is not well behaved in general.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c40e91be91c67bcba359bd1c9531ece42d8ea48b1314bb00520344419021a2a1", "unit_id": "tag:03OF:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "03OF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$U = S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-local-final-object}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-final-object}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b4e9ea310103fdfa34c4aa924d33a63f1bd58a859ea4000c6a6f035ce85ea6af", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a5c33b8546372b5a76180b37f176c534c848d562e44b0d6cffc542b68c50879b", "source_text": "In the case where <MATH_0001> has a final object, e.g.<SPACE_0001><MATH_0002>, it\nsuffices to check the condition of the definition for\n<MATH_0003> in the above statement. See\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:81c44cecb8c8a1f18dc23a5de92ccc746e7c8efab9628a34eea8ab40fd95a5f9", "unit_id": "tag:03OI:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "03OF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Sch/S$", "MATH_0005": "$T \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$S/S$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0013": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{F}^a$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0016": "$S$", "OWNARGEND_0001": "]\n\\label{theorem-quasi-coherent}\n", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}[", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1c63163643729f795c07539f662a1e9c0838758020a2eea8bfe09b0828e87bd2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3c2cea4c2631cb1a519f5d423c82f963af561c3fd9411dd4c887a428ae7037f7", "source_text": "Meta theorem on quasi-coherent sheaves<OWNARGEND_0001>Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a site. Assume that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the underlying category <MATH_0003> is a\nfull subcategory of <MATH_0004>,\n<STRUCT_0003> any Zariski covering of <MATH_0005>\ncan be refined by a covering of <MATH_0006>,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0007> is an object of <MATH_0008>,\n<STRUCT_0005> every covering of <MATH_0009> is an fpqc covering of schemes.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nThen the presheaf <MATH_0010> is a sheaf on <MATH_0011> and\nany quasi-coherent <MATH_0012>-module on <MATH_0013>\nis of the form <MATH_0014> for some quasi-coherent sheaf\n<MATH_0015> on <MATH_0016>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7a1143e35be53f47739bba753b88894af215f7f490d380f9844a489a69cb3508", "unit_id": "tag:03OJ:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03OF", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-descent-quasi-coherent}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{descent-proposition-equivalence-quasi-coherent}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3373d69d1a771d1b240d3f94798edce7e161caf54de4b2de49dd8524c8dc1502", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:20d35d26091dadeb0d2658334c75ee508be82d7724071ee9106becd822d161f8", "source_text": "After some formal arguments this is exactly Theorem\n<REF_0001>. Details omitted. In\nDescent, Proposition <REF_0002>\nwe prove a more precise version of the theorem for the\nbig Zariski, fppf, <ACCENT_0001>tale, smooth, and syntomic sites of <MATH_0001>,\nas well as the small Zariski and <ACCENT_0002>tale sites of <MATH_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c9227928fad2cd10bdd4935a0c416ea6dc49da45dcc45837e4895165132e099d", "unit_id": "tag:03OJ:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03OF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$S_\\etale$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{descent-section-quasi-coherent-sheaves}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{descent-section-quasi-coherent-cohomology}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{descent-section-quasi-coherent-sheaves-bis}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{theorem-quasi-coherent}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:da0bb14144a6b454772bd18283a841d5dd85b8b1c91f9f2fcb4f60abb258b59b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3f5f9d61f649c665a1582b8257e4f580809b19a07a70ab49249d9f51549b3829", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn other words, there is no difference between quasi-coherent\nmodules on the scheme <MATH_0001> and quasi-coherent <MATH_0002>-modules\non sites <MATH_0003> as in the theorem. More precise statements\nfor the big and small sites <MATH_0004>, <MATH_0005>, etc\ncan be found in Descent, Sections\n<REF_0001>,\n<REF_0002>, and\n<REF_0003>.\nIn this chapter we will sometimes refer to a\n``site as in Theorem <REF_0004>''\nin order to conveniently state results which hold in any of those\nsituations.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:75be43fc3bed5ffe3983c69a92ed81c700fa01985f823033109c1569178bb488", "unit_id": "tag:03OF:prose-0004"}
